<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Sharing on OpenSubsonic</title><link>https://opensubsonic.github.io/pr/265/categories/sharing/</link><description>Recent content in Sharing on OpenSubsonic</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://opensubsonic.github.io/pr/265/categories/sharing/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>createShare</title><link>https://opensubsonic.github.io/pr/265/docs/endpoints/createshare/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://opensubsonic.github.io/pr/265/docs/endpoints/createshare/</guid><description>&lt;p>&lt;code>http://your-server/rest/createShare&lt;/code> Since &lt;a href="../../subsonic-versions">1.6.0&lt;/a>&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Creates a public URL that can be used by anyone to stream music or video from the server. The URL is short and suitable for posting on Facebook, Twitter etc. Note: The user must be authorized to share (see Settings &amp;gt; Users &amp;gt; User is allowed to share files with anyone).&lt;/p>
&lt;h3 id="parameters">Parameters&lt;/h3>
&lt;table>
 &lt;thead>
 &lt;tr>
 &lt;th>Parameter&lt;/th>
 &lt;th>Req.&lt;/th>
 &lt;th>OpenS.&lt;/th>
 &lt;th>Default&lt;/th>
 &lt;th>Comment&lt;/th>
 &lt;/tr>
 &lt;/thead>
 &lt;tbody>
 &lt;tr>
 &lt;td>&lt;code>id&lt;/code>&lt;/td>
 &lt;td>&lt;strong>Yes&lt;/strong>&lt;/td>
 &lt;td>&lt;/td>
 &lt;td>&lt;/td>
 &lt;td>ID of a song, album or video to share. Use one &lt;code>id&lt;/code> parameter for each entry to share.&lt;/td>
 &lt;/tr>
 &lt;tr>
 &lt;td>&lt;code>description&lt;/code>&lt;/td>
 &lt;td>No&lt;/td>
 &lt;td>&lt;/td>
 &lt;td>&lt;/td>
 &lt;td>A user-defined description that will be displayed to people visiting the shared media.&lt;/td>
 &lt;/tr>
 &lt;tr>
 &lt;td>&lt;code>expires&lt;/code>&lt;/td>
 &lt;td>No&lt;/td>
 &lt;td>&lt;/td>
 &lt;td>&lt;/td>
 &lt;td>The time at which the share expires. Given as milliseconds since 1970.&lt;/td>
 &lt;/tr>
 &lt;/tbody>
&lt;/table>
&lt;h3 id="example">Example&lt;/h3>


&lt;div class="alert alert-primary" role="alert">


 &lt;code>http://your-server/rest/createShare.view?id=123&amp;amp;u=demo&amp;amp;p=demo&amp;amp;v=1.13.0&amp;amp;c=AwesomeClientName&amp;amp;f=json&lt;/code>

&lt;/div>

&lt;h3 id="result">Result&lt;/h3>
&lt;p>A &lt;a href="../../responses/subsonic-response">&lt;code>subsonic-response&lt;/code>&lt;/a> element with a nested &lt;a href="../../responses/shares">&lt;code>shares&lt;/code>&lt;/a> element on success. Which in turns contains a single &lt;a href="../../responses/share">&lt;code>share&lt;/code>&lt;/a> element for the newly created share&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>deleteShare</title><link>https://opensubsonic.github.io/pr/265/docs/endpoints/deleteshare/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://opensubsonic.github.io/pr/265/docs/endpoints/deleteshare/</guid><description>&lt;p>&lt;code>http://your-server/rest/deleteShare&lt;/code> Since &lt;a href="../../subsonic-versions">1.6.0&lt;/a>&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Deletes an existing share.&lt;/p>
